-- title:
--   Deformation over W₀[[X]] of a supersingular curve with monomial j
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $q$, and $E_0$ an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ whose formal group $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$ (the formal group law $\mathrm{formalGroupLawFixed}$ attached to the Weierstrass data of $E_0$) satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with the zero ideal as the ambient ideal there is a unit $u\in k[[X]]$ with $q$-th iterate series $\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q$ (the $q$-fold substitution of the group law into itself, $[q]$) equal to $u$ times the Drinfeld divisor series `drinfeldDivisor q 0 0` of the pair $(0,0)$. Let $W_0$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, and let $\mathrm{res}_0\colon W_0\to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal. Then there exist: a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E$ over $W_0[[X]]$ with $\mathcal E.\Delta$ a unit, whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0\circ\mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is $E_0$; a formal group law $F^u$ over $W_0[[X]]$ which is commutative, whose underlying two-variable series is $\mathcal E.\mathrm{formalGroupLawFixed}$, and such that the image of that series under $\mathrm{res}_0\circ\mathrm{constantCoeff}$ is the series of $E_0.\mathrm{formalGroup}$; writing $\gamma:=\mathrm{coeff}_q(F^u.\mathrm{nthSeries}\,q)\in W_0[[X]]$, one has $\mathrm{coeff}_1(\gamma)-1$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, and a unit $u_1\in W_0[[X]]$ with $\gamma-u_1X\in qW_0[[X]]$; finally $a_0\in W_0$, an exponent $e\ge 1$ and a unit $u_2\in W_0[[X]]$ with $\mathcal E.\mathrm{jOfUnit}-a_0=u_2X^e$, where $\mathrm{jOfUnit}$ is the $j$-invariant of $\mathcal E$ formed from the unit discriminant.
--
--   This provides the one-parameter Weierstrass deformation over $W_0[[X]]$ of a supersingular elliptic curve in characteristic $q\ge 5$ that is used as the geometric input on the supersingular locus: the congruence $\gamma\equiv u_1X \pmod q$ says that the Hasse invariant of the family is a unit times the parameter, and the $j$-invariant of the family is a constant plus a unit times a power of the parameter. It is cited in the construction of the level moduli package, via [`ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_mem_span_and_map_j0_sub_algebraMap_eq_mul_pow_of_factorsThrough_of_five_le_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_mem_span_and_map_j0_sub_algebraMap_eq_mul_pow_of_factorsThrough_of_five_le_gamma0Pow), and by a variant in which the monomial $u_2X^e$ is replaced by an evaluation.
